s, excellent computer skills, pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone, can be grumpy, can be uncooperative.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills, creates positive atmosphere with crew, 100% reliable, keeps calm in crisis.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner, arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe have also from Agent 1: crew cooperation notes: C positive atmosphere, B grumpy/uncooperative, D arrogant/loner, A no explicit.\n\nWe need to evaluate criteria: reliability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, stress resilience, decision quality, attention accuracy, professional communication, adaptability, etc.\n\nLet's weigh each candidate:\n\n- A: strong technical (anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision), leadership (crew cooperation potential). Weaknesses: unfriendly, unhealthy (health reliability), not good at criticism, unorganized, show\u2011off, not open to new ideas. No explicit stress resilience or calmness. No explicit decision quality. Reliability questionable due to health and attitude.\n\n- B: high reliability (conscientious), stress handling, weather assessment (technical), computer skills (technical). Weaknesses: pretentious, wrong tone, grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation). No explicit decision quality, attention accuracy, adaptability.\n\n- C: 100% reliability, calm in crisis, quick correct decisions, excellent attention, positive crew atmosphere (cooperation), puts concern for others (responsibility), but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability), egocentric may affect crew dynamics. But overall strong on many criteria.\n\n- D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, responds to unexpected events (stress resilience), but moody, loner, arrogant, weak leadership, no explicit reliability, decision quality unknown, attention unknown.\n\nThus Candidate C seems strongest overall: reliability, calmness, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation. The concerns (communication difficulty, egocentric, unwillingness to further education) are notable but perhaps less critical than B's uncooperative behavior and A's health/unreliability.\n\nThus as agent_3, I should likely support Candidate C as the best overall fit, aligning with Agent 2's recommendation. However, we need to consider that Agent 1 now recommends A, but we can argue why C remains best.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: Agent 1's points about A's strengths and concerns, Agent 2's points about C's strengths and concerns, and maybe Agent 3's earlier vote for B. We can now update our vote to Candidate C, providing reasoning.\n\nThus our PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Agent 2 that Candidate C remains the strongest overall, because ...\". Provide evidence: 100% reliability, calm in crisis, quick correct decisions, excellent attention, positive crew atmosphere. Contrast with A's health and criticism issues, B's uncooperative, D's moody/loner.\n\nThus METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
